+## `GetClientCapabilities() -> a{sv}`
+
+Returns the WebAuthn [client capabilities][def-client-capability], so that
+the portal can answer `getClientCapabilities()` and
+`isUserVerifyingPlatformAuthenticatorAvailable()`. Each value is a boolean,
+and the keys are the capability names in snake_case:
+
+- `conditional_create`, `conditional_get`: always false for now.
+- `hybrid_transport`: the hybrid transport is available.
+- `passkey_platform_authenticator`: a user-verifying platform provider or
+  the hybrid transport is available.
+- `user_verifying_platform_authenticator`: a platform provider answered
+  `GetInfo()` with at least one user verification method. A locked
+  provider counts, since the user is asked to unlock it.
+- `related_origins`: requests are validated with related origin requests.
+- `signal_all_accepted_credentials`, `signal_current_user_details`,
+  `signal_unknown_credential`: always false for now.
+
+[def-client-capability]: https://www.w3.org/TR/webauthn-3/#enumdef-clientcapability
+
